    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Good call, when I suggested removing `immediate` it was under the assumption we always called it with `true`, but indeed this branch is called with false. I wonder if instead of the `setUserTokenToSearch` having a delay, `setUserTokenToSearch` should be called with a delay inside this callback to make it clearer",
    "commit_id": "0bd80c0b93f017e23719d7b1938364db775cf02d",
    "created_at": "2024-11-20T09:01:15Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -264,46 +245,14 @@ export function createInsightsMiddleware<\n             if (existingToken && existingToken !== userToken) {\n               instantSearchInstance.scheduleSearch();\n             }\n-\n-            currentTokenType = tokenType;\n-          }\n-\n-          // the authenticated user token cannot be overridden by a user or anonymous token\n-          // for instant search query requests\n-          if (\n-            currentTokenType &&\n-            currentTokenType === 'authenticated' &&\n-            tokenType === 'default' &&\n-            !unsetAuthenticatedUserToken\n-          ) {\n-            return;\n           }\n \n-          // Delay the token application to the next render cycle\n-          if (!immediate) {\n-            setTimeout(applyToken, 0);\n-          } else {\n-            applyToken();\n-          }",
